/**
 * CLEO Steps to Justice — plain-language guidance for the claim-type profiles.
 *
 * GENERATED by scripts/.../genCleoSources.mjs from a crawl of the Steps to Justice
 * topic index. Regenerate rather than hand-edit.
 *
 * *** WHY CLEO AT ALL, WHEN THE STATUTES ARE ALREADY VENDORED ***
 *
 * The statutes say what the law is. They do not say what a claim type IS in words
 * a person recognises, and several things a profile must state have no statutory
 * source at all — what a collection agency actually does, what to bring to a
 * hearing, what "as is" means on a used car. CLAUDE.md §2 lists CLEO as an
 * acceptable source, and the drafter may quote it; where neither a statute nor
 * CLEO states something, the profile says we have no verified guidance rather than
 * inventing it.
 *
 * *** WHAT IS HERE, AND WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT ***
 *
 * Crawled: 306 distinct question pages across the Small Claims, debt and consumer,
 * housing, employment, tribunal and provincial-offences topics.
 *
 * Vendored here: the Small Claims court topic in full, debt and consumer rights in
 * full, and the human-rights, provincial-offences and finding-a-lawyer pages that
 * forum checks route to — plus seven topic landing pages so a forum check can cite
 * a tribunal's own description of what it handles.
 *
 * NOT vendored yet, and recorded so the number is honest: 105 employment-and-work,
 * 88 housing-law and 12 income-assistance question pages. Those topics are mostly
 * about procedure at another tribunal DURING a relationship, which claim-type
 * profiles reach only as a forum check — and a forum check needs the tribunal's
 * landing page, not eighty pages of its procedure. Vendoring them now would add
 * 205 sources that nothing cites, each re-fetched on every drift check and each
 * able to go stale, for no content gain. They are a later slice, not a decision
 * that they do not matter.
 *
 * *** EVERY ENTRY PROVES IT LANDED ON THE RIGHT PAGE ***
 *
 * mustContain carries two distinctive words from the page's own slug. Requiring
 * only "Steps to Justice" would pass on any CLEO page at all, which is the same
 * failure as the e-Laws chapter id returning the wrong schedule.
 */

